v. 90 armor component\"><img alt=\"Lv. 90 armor component\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Rare Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Rare_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203235927\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Gold Angel\"><img alt=\"Gold Angel\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Horror of Antiquity\"><img alt=\"Horror of Antiquity\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Diamond Ring\"><img alt=\"Diamond Ring\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As we enter, Shantotto decides we're just who she needs. An option box pops up but we can't change the option and have to agree to help her. There's more Manikins down here that are running amok, and she needs us to take care of them.\n</p><p>Multhchain at C4 to get all the enemies present here. The blue emblem is awesome a Booster x5 emblem. There's eight enemies here with the Party piece, so if you brought along a KP Gambler, this is the time and place to use it.\n</p><p>First foe on the chopping block, a Level 62 Fallacious Wanderer. Next is a Level 61 Horror of Antiquity, naturally from the level it's much weaker than the Expert one from before. Then comes the Party - Level 63 Transient Lion, Level 63 Capricious Thief, Level 63 Ephemeral Vision, and finally a Level 79 Lady of Antiquity. \n</p><p>Then comes one of the Expert enemies, a new one, a Fallacious Giant, Gilgamesh's Manikin. He has Cross Slash, a low-ranged chop attack on the ground, Whirlwind Slash, a slow long-ranged dive forward, Wind Slash, which fires a blast of wind, Double Trouble, a very quick but very short-ranged attack, Tsubamegeshi, a diving chop forward, and Electrocute, which summons a lightning bolt around you. His HP attacks are Death Claw, a two-hit charge attack forward similar to Cloud's Cross-Slash but with one less hit and more horizontal range, Jump, which is just like Kain's but with longer lag on impact and no charging, Hurricane, a close-range aerial spin attack, and Missile, which fires a large homing missile at you that explodes. His summon, appropriately, is Gilgamesh, which randomly triples his Bravery or reduces it to 1. His Assist is a Fallacious Tree. He's not too dangerous as long as you don't get close, aside from Double Trouble and Hurricane his attacks are easy to anticipate and dodge or block, once you get the hang of him of course, feel free to retry.\n</p><p>The last enemy is a Level 89 Counterfeit Wraith, not sure what her summon is, she never used it. \n</p><p>The two normal chests have a Gold Angel and a Diamond Ring. Save this, it increases the AP we earn x4, you can use it at the gateway I mentioned last chapter, with the accessories protected emblem. The silver chalice is a Moogle Chalice, it will instantly double your earned KP, like a KP Bonus.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d6/Dissidia_opened_chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204002016\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Delusory Warlock/Lv. 90 armor component\"><img alt=\"Delusory Warlock/Lv. 90 armor component\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissidia opened chest.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissidia_opened_chest.png\" 