scription image\" title=\"Chain Skill\"><img alt=\"Chain Skill\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204003912\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Lady of Antiquity\"><img alt=\"Lady of Antiquity\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"25\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Expert Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/25?cb=20110204003912\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235927\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Lv. 90 armor component\"><img alt=\"Lv. 90 armor component\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Rare Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Rare_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203235927\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Gabranth asks how we don't give in as we arrive. There are two options to chain enemies here, a Multichain at E4 or G4, the former gives an Initial BRV Booster, the latter gives Stage BRV Boost. I prefer the second myself. However, only do this if you have a Multichain to spare, the skill chests up to this point may have rewarded a second one. I got <i>very</i> lucky and got a new one from the chest here after I used my only Multichain, yay!\n</p><p>The opposition is the Party piece, a Level 90 Phantasmal Harlequin with Tiamat and a Phantasmal Girl Assist, then a Level 91 Capricious Reaper with Calcabrina and a Capricious Thief Assist. The rest are a Level 97 Delusory Dragoon with Alexander and a Fleeting Flash Assist, a Level 81 Fallacious Giant with the Gilgamesh summon, a Level 79 Lady of Antiquity with Carbuncle, and a Level 79 Warrior of Antiquity with Zalera.\n</p><p>Ya know, I get that the Antiquity manikins, being the manikins of people from the pre-12 cycles, are a focus in these gateways, it makes sense in a way. But seriously, couldn't you guys get a bit more creative? I personally would have put the hero manikins in the first one, since it's a paradise for those who win the war, and in here put the villain manikins as losers who have been banished, or put the six 12th cycle heroes in. It's the final areas developers, you've shown us all the characters and given us access to almost all the equipment types, the time to be more creative is now!\n</p><p>The two chests have a Friendship Resin and a random skill again.\n<br style=\"clear:both\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#1