e-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20121006224522\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Party Battle\"><img alt=\"Party Battle\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Party Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/30?cb=20121006224522\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235927\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Lv. 90 armor component\"><img alt=\"Lv. 90 armor component\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Rare Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Rare_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203235927\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20121006224522\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Party Battle\"><img alt=\"Party Battle\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Party Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/30?cb=20121006224522\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/11/D012_Silver_Moogle_Chalice.png/revision/latest?cb=20121006224139\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"KP Silver Cup\"><img alt=\"KP Silver Cup\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"21\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Silver Moogle Chalice.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Silver_Moogle_Chalice.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/11/D012_Silver_Moogle_Chalice.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/21?cb=20121006224139\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As we enter this floor, Gabranth tells us of how he fought for the gods with pride and fought Shantotto, but his pride meant nothing to the gods and when he was deemed no longer useful, he was discarded to this hellhole.\n</p><p>Multichain at F2 to get all but one enemy. This is the time to use that KP Gambler kiddies! I also used a Blind skill from a chest in here.\n</p><p>The first Party, a Level 81 Phantasmal Harlequin with Tiamat and a Phantasmal Girl Assist, a Level 82 Imaginary Champion also with Tiamat and an Imaginary Soldier Assist, and a Level 82 Transient Witch with a Transient Lion and an unknown summon. The second Party is a Level 81 Delusory Warlock with Giant of Babil and a Delusory Knight Assist, and a Level 81 Fallacious Tree with a Fallacious Wanderer Assist and a summon he never used on me. Then come the three Experts, a Level 80 Counterfeit Wraith with a Counterfeit Youth and Atomos, and a Level 80 Imitation Despot with Iron Giant and an Imitation Liegeman Assist. The one we missed at B4 is a False Stalwart with a False Hero and Behemoth. Be warned, fighting it forces us on an Items Disabled red emblem, so bring a good Summon.\n</p><p>Also, I put Prishe back in the lead, she and the other party members are Level 93, Lightning is 97.\n</p><p>The two chests have a random skill and an Iifa Leaf. Also, if you have any KP Bonus items, use them now, I had 560 KP after the Chalice.\n</p><p>As we reach the final level, Gabranth realizes the world above holds meaning for us, if we're fighting so hard to get back.\n</p><p>The last two enemies are a Level 79 Warrior of Antiquity with Zalera and an Idle Sky Pirate, and a Level 80 Horror of Antiquity with a Lady of Antiquity and Hecatoncheir. The red chest is another enemy in disguise, a Level 97 Idle Sky Pirate with Cactuar and a Warrior of Antiquity Assist.\n</p><p>You now have an important dilemma to deal with, you can get those two chests with Level 90 trade accessories, but you have to fight your Assist to do it. The choice is yours. The normal chest has a random piece of the Elemental Archfiend equipment, a four-piece set that grants a boost to your Bravery during block, dodge, quickmove and stage destruction. It also sucks, largely due to its level. Square-Enix, if you're going to make an equipment set that forces us to run through a dungeon of Level 80 enemies at least four times to get, we're probably past the point that Level 60 equipment is useful.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"The_Warrior.27s_Judgment\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Warrior's_Judgment\">The Warrior's Judgment</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Warrior&#39;s Judgment\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_23?action=edit&amp;section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Warrior&#39;s Judgment\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Gabranth_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Gabranth (Dissidia PSP)\">Gabranth</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6f/GabranthDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110706095437\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"GabranthDissidiaRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"146\" height=\"200\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"GabranthDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-image-key=\"GabranthDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6f/GabranthDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/146?cb=20110706095437\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">9,290\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">90\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">939\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Enrage, Relentless Lunge, Aero, Rupture, Dual Rend, Vortex of Judgement\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Execution, Innocence, Hatred\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Omega\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">3/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As we reach the exit, Gabranth understands we still wish to return, so now there's one final test. Time for the Judge Magister to do what he does best - dispense judgement upon us and carry out sentencing. \n</p><p>Gabranth is a <i>much</i> more competent opponent than Shantotto. You've probably got a level advantage on him, but a much weaker one than Shantotto, since Gabranth is Level 90 to Shantotto's 70. And they gave him what is, honestly, one of the most brilliant accessory builds of any enemy - a Puppeteer's Wheel. Yes, the same one Terra had in her boss fights that let her stay in EX Mode the entire fight. Ho boy. Gabranth also has an Attractorb and Hyper Ring hooked up to five EX Mode boosters, giving him a 3.7x booster as long as he's in EX Mode, and after 30 seconds pass in the fight, off go two more boosters, taking him to 8.3x. And to finish up, he's got an Idle Sky Pirate Assist and the Omega Summon. About the only way he could be worse is if they gave him an Iifa Dew or Leaf, or a Muscle Belt instead of the Hyper Ring. Fortunately he doesn't have EX Critical Boost or else most all of his attacks would be critical hits.\n</p><p>I hope you came into the fight with a full EX Gauge, because with that pumped up Attractorb he won't be leaving any EX Force for you. Between that and the Puppeteer's Wheel, Gabranth is going to be in EX Mode the entire fight unless you knock him out of it with an Assist Break...unless you killed your Assist to get access to those chests. Oops. As well, the fight is in Edge of Madness Ω, where the Bravery pool is constantly in flux from several thousand to a few hundred Bravery. Time your Break well or else you'll have nothing to show for your effort in wearing him down.\n</p><p>You know how Gabranth's attacks work from his manikins, he's just a much bigger, beefier version of them, and is fought in a very small arena so you have nowhere to run or hide from him. His accessories are going to give him a big damage buff so I hope you can block on a whim because if he connects he's going to hurt, and know which of his attacks can't be blocked. And of course, don't forget he's going to be recovering HP the entire fight thanks to Regen. He's a very powerful, very <i>smart</i> opponent, and he can thrash you easily. If you didn't kill your Assist, charge it up and get in an Assist attack to EX Break him and end his EX Mode, then don't let him sit still long enough to charge it back up. If not, then it's just a battle of pure brawn. Good luck kiddies!\n</p><p>After he's beaten, Gabranth shows us the exit, but warns that we will face despair and loss, but we can't let it break our spirits and have to hold onto hope.\n</p><p>With the two optional gateways completed, it's time to head to our actual objective. As before, go restock your chain skills and prepare to enter the Chasm in the Rotting Land.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/000-creator/southern-areas/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 22\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 4\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 6\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Light to All\">Light to All</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/013-light/prologue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 9\">Prologue</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 10\">Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 11\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 12\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 13\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 14\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 15\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 16\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-8/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 17\">8</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-9/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 18\">9</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-10/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 19\">10</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/epilogue-part-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 20\">Epilogue Part 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/epilogue-part-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 21\">Part 2</a><hr />\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/000-creator/chasm-of-earth-and-flying-castle/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 24\">Next page</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" valign=\"top\">\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<caption><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Confessions_of_the_Creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Confessions of the Creator\">Confessions of the Creator</a></b>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/000-creator/southern-areas/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 22\">Part 1</a> - <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part 2</strong> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/chasm-of-earth-and-flying-castle/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 24\">Part 3</a> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/gaia-and-bahamut-isles/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 25\">Part 4</a> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/land-of-discord-and-feral-chaos/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 26\">Part 5</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" valign=\"top\">\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<caption><b>Extras</b>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/reports/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Reports\">The Reports</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260902040224\nCache expiry: 1209600\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.116 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.135 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 3588/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 31947/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 13571/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 7/100\nExpensive parser function count: 2/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   34.323      1 -total\n 67.73%   23.246      8 Template:Map_D012\n 19.42%    6.667      1 Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Nav\n 13.64%    4.683      1 Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Nav2\n  6.53%    2.240      2 Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Enemies\n  4.04%    1.387      4 Template:Clear\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_finalfantasy:pcache:idhash:157240-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries an